From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EdenEast <edenofest@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:23:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: trust identical .envrc files in git worktrees

Add a `git_worktrees` option to the `[whitelist]` section of
direnv.toml. When enabled, an .envrc file in a linked git worktree is
allowed if it is byte-for-byte identical to the .envrc file at the same
relative path in the main worktree, and that file is allowed.

direnv keys trust on the absolute path of the .envrc file, so every new
worktree needs its own `direnv allow` even when nothing changed. This
option removes that step while still asking for approval when a branch
changes its .envrc.

Trust does not chain: the main worktree file is checked against the
deny list, allow list and path whitelists only.
